  {
   "index": 19,
   "tag": "section×2",
   "id": "install-scientific-python-packages",
   "landmarks": [
    "role=main",
    "section",
    "section",
    "section"
   ],
   "textLength": 939,
   "text": "… install scientific Python packages?¶\nA number of scientific Python packages have complex binary dependencies, and\naren’t currently easy to install using pip directly.\nIt will often be easier for users to install these packages by\nother means\nrather than attempting to install them with pip.\nSee also\nPython Packaging User Guide: Installing Scientific Packages\n… work with multiple versions of Pytho",
